<.docs_layout active_guide="app-shell">
  <.doc_heading
    title="App shell"
    description="The whole shell of a signed-in app: a collapsible sidebar on wide screens, a pinned top row, bottom dock and More sheet on phones, search, the account menu, and one scroll region for the page."
  />

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-12">
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Desktop</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        A live app in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;.app_shell&gt;</code>.
        Click into it, then try <kbd class="kbd kbd-sm">⌘K</kbd>
        (search, filter, Enter), <kbd class="kbd kbd-sm">⌘B</kbd>
        or the grab strip on the sidebar's edge (the icon rail, remembered across reloads),
        the account menu, an order (Esc goes back), and scroll a page to see its header pin.
        Scroll the sidebar down and pick a page: it keeps its place.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border shadow-sm">
        <iframe
          id="shell-desktop"
          src={ShadcnDaisyuiDemoWeb.ShellPreview.path("home")}
          title="App shell on a wide screen"
          class="block h-[40rem] w-full"
          loading="lazy"
        >
        </iframe>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Phone</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The same app below 48rem: the top row (your app's slot, then search) stays pinned and the
        page header pins under it; the dock holds four destinations and More, which opens the
        whole navigation, the footer items and the account. No hamburger.
      </p>
      <div class="flex justify-center">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] border-8 border-base-300 shadow-sm">
          <iframe
            id="shell-phone"
            src={ShadcnDaisyuiDemoWeb.ShellPreview.path("order")}
            title="App shell on a phone"
            class="block h-[44rem] w-[390px] max-w-full"
            loading="lazy"
          >
          </iframe>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Usage</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        In your
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">Layouts.app/1</code>
        for signed-in pages. Brand pickers, permission checks, routes and copy stay in your app:
        pass them in through the attributes and slots.
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="heex"
        code={
          ~S'''
          <.app_shell
            nav={MyAppWeb.Navigation.groups(@current_scope)}
            more={MyAppWeb.Navigation.phone_groups(@current_scope)}
            active={@active}
            wide={@wide}
            fill={@fill}
            search="search"
            environment={Application.get_env(:my_app, :environment_label)}
            person={%{name: @current_scope.user.name, email: @current_scope.user.email}}
          >
            <:header>
              <.app_shell_heading id="app-heading" icon="hero-cube" title="Acme" subtitle="Operations" tip="Acme · Operations" />
            </:header>
            <:phone_header>
              <span class="app-shell-tile"><.icon name="hero-cube" /></span>
              <span class="text-sm font-semibold">Acme</span>
            </:phone_header>
            <:footer_item id="whats-new-open" icon="hero-megaphone" label="What's new" phx-click={show_modal("whats-new")} />
            <:account_item id="account" icon="hero-user-circle" navigate={~p"/account"}>Account</:account_item>
            <:account_item id="notifications" icon="hero-bell" navigate={~p"/notifications"}>Notifications</:account_item>
            <:account_item id="support" icon="hero-lifebuoy" soon divider>Support</:account_item>
            <:account_item id="feedback" icon="hero-chat-bubble-left-ellipsis" soon>Feedback</:account_item>
            <:account_item id="sign-out" icon="hero-arrow-right-start-on-rectangle"
              href={~p"/sign-out"} method="delete" destructive divider>
              Sign out
            </:account_item>
            {render_slot(@inner_block)}
          </.app_shell>

          <.command id="search" label="Search" placeholder="Search pages">
            <:item :for={page <- @pages} id={"search-page-" <> page.id} group="Pages" icon={page.icon} navigate={page.path}>
              {page.label}
            </:item>
          </.command>
          <.flash_group flash={@flash} />
          '''
        }
      />
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The navigation is groups of items, the shape a
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">Navigation</code>
        module filtered by permissions returns.
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">short</code>
        is the dock label (optional).
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">bar</code>
        defaults to the first four items of <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">more</code>,
        and <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">more</code>
        to <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">nav</code>
        (leave desktop-only pages out of it).
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="elixir"
        code={
          ~S'''
          [
            %{label: nil, items: [%{id: "home", label: "Home", short: "Home", path: "/", icon: "hero-home"}]},
            %{label: "Sales", items: [
              %{id: "orders", label: "Orders", short: "Orders", path: "/orders", icon: "hero-shopping-cart"},
              %{id: "customers", label: "Customers", short: "People", path: "/customers", icon: "hero-users"}
            ]}
          ]
          '''
        }
      />
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Page header</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Every page starts with
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;.page_header&gt;</code>
        (from your <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">CoreComponents</code>),
        so the breadcrumb, title and actions sit in the same place on every page, pinned while
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">#main</code>
        scrolls. The breadcrumb shows from 48rem; on a record the list is a link and Esc goes there.
        Open an order in the previews above to try it.
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="heex"
        code={
          ~S'''
          <.page_header crumbs={[%{label: "Sales"}, %{label: "Orders", path: ~p"/orders"}, %{label: "#1042"}]}>
            #1042
            <:badge><.badge variant="outline">Paid</.badge></:badge>
            <:actions>
              <.button variant="outline" size="sm" navigate={~p"/orders"}>Cancel</.button>
              <.button size="sm">Save</.button>
            </:actions>
          </.page_header>
          '''
        }
      />
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Keep a thin wrapper in your
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">CoreComponents</code>
        that computes the crumbs from your navigation:
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="elixir"
        code={
          ~S'''
          attr :page, :string, required: true
          attr :current, :string, default: nil
          # ...the rest of page_header's attrs and slots

          def page_header(assigns) do
            assigns = assign(assigns, :crumbs, MyAppWeb.Navigation.crumbs(assigns.page, assigns.current))
            ShadcnDaisyui.CoreComponents.page_header(assigns)
          end
          '''
        }
      />
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">List and record pages</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        A list page is a
        <a href={~p"/docs/components/table-toolbar"} class="link link-primary">table toolbar</a>
        over a <a href={~p"/docs/components/data-table"} class="link link-primary">data table</a>
        in an
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">
          &lt;.app_shell wide fill&gt;
        </code>
        page: the table takes the space left and only its body scrolls. A record page adds
        <a href={~p"/docs/components/record-tabs"} class="link link-primary">record tabs</a>
        and a <a href={~p"/docs/components/section-nav"} class="link link-primary">section nav</a>
        in the page header's <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;:below&gt;</code>,
        and <a href={~p"/docs/components/table-card"} class="link link-primary">table cards</a>
        for its rows. Open Orders in the previews above; on the dev server
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">/lab/data-table</code>
        runs both in a LiveView.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Command dialog</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The shell's search is a <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">&lt;.command&gt;</code>.
        Items navigate, link, submit a form or run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">phx-click</code>;
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">shortcut</code>
        is its Cmd/Ctrl letter (⌘K by default,
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">nil</code>
        for none). This one has none (⌘K on this site opens the docs search):
      </p>
      <div class="flex min-h-32 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-border p-8">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline" phx-click={show_modal("shell-switcher")}>
          <.icon name="hero-arrows-right-left" class="size-4" /> Switch team
        </button>
        <.command
          id="shell-switcher"
          label="Switch team"
          placeholder="Search teams"
          shortcut={nil}
        >
          <:item
            :for={team <- ["Operations", "Field", "Finance", "Marketing"]}
            group="Teams"
            icon="hero-user-group"
            href={~p"/docs/app-shell"}
          >
            {team}
          </:item>
        </.command>
      </div>
      <.code_block
        language="heex"
        code={
          ~S'''
          <.button variant="outline" phx-click={show_modal("team-switcher")}>Switch team</.button>
          <.command id="team-switcher" label="Switch team" placeholder="Search teams" shortcut={nil}>
            <:item :for={team <- @teams} group="Teams" icon="hero-user-group" href={~p"/teams/#{team}"}>
              {team.name}
            </:item>
            <:item group="Locations" icon="hero-map-pin" form="location-form" name="location" value="all">
              All locations
            </:item>
          </.command>
          '''
        }
      />
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Setup</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The hooks (<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">ShadcnCommand</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">ShadcnStickyTop</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">ShadcnPageBack</code>)
        come with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">Hooks</code>, and the
        shell's events (<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">shadcn:toggle-sidebar</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">shadcn:show-dialog</code>) with
        the module itself; all of it works under a strict <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">script-src</code>. The root
        layout sets the theme and the sidebar's state before first paint;
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">
          mix shadcn_daisyui.install
        </code>
        and
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">
          mix shadcn_daisyui.upgrade
        </code>
        add the sidebar line to it. The whole script:
      </p>
      <.code_block
        language="root.html.heex"
        code={
          ~S'''
          <script nonce={assigns[:csp_nonce]}>
            (() => {
              const root = document.documentElement;
              const systemTheme = () => matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "shadcn-dark" : "shadcn";
              // instant swap: transitions off only while the theme changes
              const setTheme = (theme) => {
                root.classList.add("theme-transition");
                if (theme === "system") {
                  localStorage.removeItem("phx:theme");
                  root.setAttribute("data-theme", systemTheme());
                  root.setAttribute("data-theme-source", "system");
                } else {
                  localStorage.setItem("phx:theme", theme);
                  root.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
                  root.setAttribute("data-theme-source", "user");
                }
                requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => root.classList.remove("theme-transition")));
              };
              setTheme(localStorage.getItem("phx:theme") || "system");
              // <.app_shell>: the sidebar's collapsed or open state, before first paint
              root.dataset.sidebar = localStorage.getItem("shadcn:sidebar") === "collapsed" ? "collapsed" : "open";
              window.addEventListener("storage", (e) => e.key === "phx:theme" && setTheme(e.newValue || "system"));
              window.addEventListener("phx:set-theme", (e) => setTheme(e.target.dataset.phxTheme));
              matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").addEventListener("change", () => {
                if (root.getAttribute("data-theme-source") === "system") setTheme("system");
              });
            })();
          </script>
          '''
        }
      />
    </section>
  </div>
</.docs_layout>
